{"content":[{"c":["GOUGING"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Common practice among the Philistines, Amorites, Babylonians, and other nations surrounding Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.16.21","r":"Judg.16.21","rawR":"Judg.16.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.16.21","value":"Judg.16.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 16:21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.25.7","r":"2Kgs.25.7","rawR":"2Kgs.25.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.25.7","value":"2Kgs.25.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 25:7"},") of forcibly removing the eyes. The practice was intended not only to disable but also to bring extreme disgrace upon the person (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.11.2","r":"1Sam.11.2","rawR":"1Sam.11.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.11.2","value":"1Sam.11.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 11:2"},"). Although the Israelites seem to have known about it from their sojourn in Egypt (",{"href":"?bref=Num.16.14","r":"Num.16.14","rawR":"Num.16.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.16.14","value":"Num.16.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 16:14"},"), there is no evidence that it was a common practice in Israel."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=CriminalLawandPunishment_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"CriminalLawandPunishment_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"CriminalLawandPunishment_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Criminal Law and Punishment"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Gouging","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jgs 16:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.16.21","rawQueryValue":"Judg.16.21","sourceRefExact":"Judg.16.21"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 25:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.25.7","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.25.7","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.25.7"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 11:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.11.2","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.11.2","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.11.2"},{"anchorText":"Nm 16:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.16.14","rawQueryValue":"Num.16.14","sourceRefExact":"Num.16.14"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"cba166cd84d9da1b2b97385b9f1f447e0d7c186ff928b44a8e129d608c6fbaad","sourceItemName":"Gouging","sourceItemOrder":193,"sourceMember":"Articles/G.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Gouging","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Gouging","title":"Gouging","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}